# Wild Panel Design System

Stack is **Go + Vue 2 + Ant Design Vue + CSS** (not React/Tailwind/Framer). Implement the brand language on this stack only.

## Brand from the wolf logo

- Primary cyan (eyes): `#00E8F0` / `--brand-cyan` / `--accent` (dark)
- Secondary violet: `#A855F7` / `--brand-violet` / `--glow`
- Ground: `#06070D` / `--brand-obsidian` / `--bg`
- Glass: blur `22px` (`--glass-blur`), ~58% opacity (`--glass-bg`), luminous borders (`--glass-border`)
- Fonts: Inter (EN) + Vazirmatn (FA) via `--font-sans`
- Icons: prefer existing Ant/`bo-icon` sprites; do not introduce a second icon system casually

## Source of truth

1. `web/assets/css/tokens.css` — all color/type/spacing/radius/glow/motion tokens
2. `web/assets/css/brand.css` — `wp-mark`, `wp-glass`, `wp-wordmark`, `wp-btn-primary`, empty/loading
3. `web/assets/css/components.css` — shell, rail, tiles, welcome
4. `web/assets/css/ant-bridge.css` — restyle Ant so every page inherits the system
5. `web/assets/css/terminal.css` — console surfaces

## Rules for every future change

- Never invent a new palette, radius scale, or shadow language.
- Prefer tokens (`var(--…)`) over hardcoded hex. Brand hex only when matching logo exactly.
- Glass is the default surface for cards, modals, dropdowns, sidebar, navbar, tables shells.
- Glow is reserved: primary buttons, focused inputs, active nav, charts, online/health status.
- Logo (`.wp-mark`) is elegant and sparse: login hero, splash/loading, empty states, sidebar, welcome, favicon — never spam it.
- Avoid gaming RGB, clutter, flat Ant-blue (`#1890ff`), and GitHub-terminal greys.
- User-facing name is **Wild Panel** only. Do not rename live host paths (`/etc/vpn-ui-*`, etc.).
- Keep CI sanity strings in sync with real UI (`Sign in to Wild Panel`, `lgt-holo`, `wp-mark`).

## When adding UI

Compose from existing primitives first. If something looks generic, restyle through tokens/ant-bridge — do not fork a one-off theme.
